Well, there're several solutions to this. The simplest one is to
install the LPS051 kit. Its the first release to support LPD.

If you can't do that, then contrary to what Microsoft says, you
actually can add the Digital Network Port to a Windows 2000 box by
simply acquiring DECPSMON.DLL and DECPSMON.HLP and putting them into
your \WINNT\SYSTEM32 directory, and then adding a registry key:

HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\Print\Monitors\Digital
Network Port

In that key, add a new string value 'Driver' containing
'DECPSMON.DLL'.

You can look at other print monitor registry entries as a sanity
check.

Works like a champ for me.

Thanks all

VC


