I am not sure which way you are counting, as there is no state where only
LED 7 stays on. A description of the status LEDs can be found at
http://www.pimpworks.org/dec/vaxarchive/hw/vs3100/3100leds.html

Things to check:

Make sure the VT320 is plugged into the PRINTER port not the serial port.
Make sure the switch next to the serial console is switched to the up
position to select the serial (printer) port as console.
Make sure your VT320 is set to the correct speed (duh.)
  Set the terminal to 9600,8,N,1 XON/XOFF

In any case your terminal should show information almost from the get-go:


KA42-A  V1.3

F...E...D...C...B...A...9...8...7...6?..5...4_..3_..2_..1?..


