Jaap:

Removing the SCSI card does intefer with booting of the system.  I
suspect one of two things, check to see if the computer is stating up in
serial mode.  Put a VT100 compatible terminal on serial port one, (usual
settings) and see if you get a SRM prompt (>>>) on the terminal.
Another problem could be the memory, what DIMMS do you have in it? 
PWS's are very fussy about memory, 168 pin, 66 or 100mhz ECC CL222 DIMMS
in matched pairs.

Good luck!

TomC

