The KZPSA is a FWD interface.  The cable configuration would vary based on
your storage component.  I have notes from a cluster installation that show
a Y cable (12-41769-01) and terminator (H879-AA) was used on the KZPSA end
(internal termination resistors removed), a long differential scsi cable
(BN21K-10) was used to connect to an HSZ50 disk array controller (through a
H885-AA Y-adapter).  The KZPSA is fine in non-clustered situations.
Remember the termination rules and check the board to see if the resistor
packs were removed.

Golden Eggs has a wealth of info on this
http://h18003.www1.hp.com/info/GECPQA/ which I recommend highly.

Cheers!

