Some items:
1, you can run this machine with a serial console. Less clutter, more
flexibility..
2, Linux does not run well (or at all?) on pmaxen. NetBSD, OpenBSD, Mach,
Sprite, OSF1, Ultrix, and 4.4BSD will run on them though. I run both Ultrix
and NetBSD  on various DECstations, both are decent. I've run OpenBSD and Mach
on them as well. In past days, NetBSD's X server was not as good as the Ultrix
one, and i still think the ultrix X is faster, but the Ultrix X server is
X11R5, which runs into some troubles trying to run new stuff sometimes.
notably, mozilla and xmms crash the dec X server.
I'd recommend checking out NetBSD, especially the 1.5 series or 1.6.

Isildur

